{"id":258044039258698,"type":"album","name":"Relationship of Command","artist":"At the Drive-In","year":2000,"weight":14,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/relationship-of-command-1.jpg","aoty":85,"aoty_user":86,"sputnik":4.42,"yt":"4Uc0uYIU_gE","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/at-the-drive-in/relationship-of-command","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/1165-at-the-drive-in-relationship-of-command.php","sputnikmusic":"https://www.sputnikmusic.com/album/1640/At-the-Drive-In-Relationship-of-Command/"},"desc":"Relationship of Command is the third studio album by American post-hardcore band At the Drive-In, released on September 12, 2000. The album combines an aggressive edge with a melodic drive, harmonious, emotive vocals, and surreal lyrics. While it continues in the alternative style of At the Drive-In's previous albums, Relationship of Command is seen as a more well-rounded album than its predecessors. Initially received positively by critics, the album is now seen not only as one of the most influential post-hardcore albums of the 2000s, but also as one of the most accomplished recent works in the wider rock spectrum. ."},"artist_ref":{"id":139648560236930,"name":"At the Drive-In","info":{"img":"https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/artist/ebb398f24bc437a03a06f44b7160f819/1000x1000-000000-80-0-0.jpg"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":31482837869539,"type":"genre","name":"Punk","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":2333,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":165379782273035,"type":"genre","name":"Hardcore [Punk]","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":714,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":237890000566646,"type":"genre","name":"Post-Hardcore","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":341,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":15546028624161,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Post-Hardcore","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":3,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":44456762010629,"name":"